WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.585
Start with the Excel template, or load a compatible CSV file.
The seven inputs are in millimetres.

00:00:06.685 --> 00:00:12.125
The nominal pegboard is three hundred by two hundred, with
sixteen columns and five rows.

00:00:13.542 --> 00:00:18.397
Change the board width to three hundred sixty millimetres and
apply the parameters.

00:00:18.497 --> 00:00:25.897
Nineteen columns now fit. The dashboard shows the width
threshold and preserves the last valid preview if an edit fails.

00:00:27.292 --> 00:00:35.552
Generate CAD model to run FreeCAD. The saved file retains the
Parameters spreadsheet and the fully constrained Master Slot
sketch.

00:00:35.652 --> 00:00:41.867
The rectangular array repeats a through cutter at each pitch.
Open 3D Orbit to inspect the result.

00:00:43.375 --> 00:00:52.205
Generate the 2D drawing to download the PDF or SVG. The sheet
shows four views, board dimensions, and the repeating slot
specification.

00:00:52.305 --> 00:00:58.760
Use the one to one DXF cut profile for exchange. The STEP file
contains the final solid.

00:00:59.083 --> 00:01:06.943
Run the three case tests. FreeCAD edits only the spreadsheet
between cases, then checks the openings on both faces of the
solid.

00:01:07.043 --> 00:01:15.328
The minimum, nominal and wider boards have one, eighty and
ninety five slots. Download the three row CSV and the detailed
JSON report.

